condition_name: Breast Cancer
condition_slug: breast_cancer
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A malignant epithelial neoplasm of the breast. It is the most commonly diagnosed cancer in women and is the leading cause of new cases of female cancers in Nigerian women.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[3]: "Breast: breast lump, bloody nipple discharge, breast or nipple ulceration","Axilla: armpit swelling, upper limb lymphoedema","Metastatic: respiratory (cough, breathlessness), liver (abdominal swelling, jaundice), bones (bone pain, pathological fracture), brain (seizures), spine (paraparesis or paraplegia), etc."
investigations[3]: "FNAC/core needle biopsy/incisional or excision biopsy: For histopathological and immunohistochemical analyses","Chest x-ray, abdominal USS, bone scan, with or withoutCT chest/abdomen: For Staging","Others: FBC, LFT, Electrolyte, Urea and Creatinine"
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[10]: "Chemotherapy - Neoadjuvant (locally advanced, locoregionally advanced, metastatic)",Adjuvants,"Combination chemotherapy (depending on immunohistochemistry, performance index, etc.). Examples: EC, AC, FEC, Docetaxel, Capecitabine, etc.","Radiotherapy - Hormonal therapy: dictated by immunohistochemistry","Tamoxifen: for premenopausal women, 20 mg daily for at least 5 years; for postmenopausal women with shifting to aromatase inhibitors later","Aromatase inhibitors: for postmenopausal women;",Anastrozole 1 mg daily,Letrozole 2.5 mg daily,Exemestane 25 mg daily,Trastuzumab for HER2 positive tumours
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[4]: "Lifestyle modifications (reduce exposure to estrogen, quit alcohol and smoking, etc)",Monthly breast self-examination,Clinical breast examination,"Periodic imaging e.g. mammogram, chest x-ray, abdominal USS, bone scan"
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[4]: Surgery,Lumpectomy/wide excision/quadrantectomy PLUS breast irradiation,"Mastectomy (Simple mastectomy with axillary clearance, modified radical mastectomy)",Breast reconstruction (early or late)
prognosis: null